<?xml version="1.0" encoding="UTF-8"?>
<task id="039" project="field-mapping-server-write-path-r1">
  <metadata>
    <title>FR-38: the search index is server-owned on every BFF write path (#2399)</title>
    <phase>2 W2 Unified RecordCreationService</phase>
    <gate>017 complete (the child-records route runs RecordCreationService step 8)</gate>
    <status>completed</status>
    <rigor>FULL</rigor>
    <rigor-reason>Modifies .cs in Sprk.Bff.Api; changes what a client may bind on create and update (security, access-adjacent: the index decides which BU's search a record lands in); adds tests at KEEP paths.</rigor-reason>
    <model-tier>sonnet</model-tier>
    <model-tier-reason>Fully specified by design §13.3 and spec FR-38: one drop before step 5, one change to step 8's source, the same drop on the BFF update paths. No open design question.</model-tier-reason>
    <effort>high</effort>
    <parallel-group>none</parallel-group>
    <parallel-safe>false</parallel-safe>
    <parallel-reason>Edits RecordCreationService.cs (one core file, W2 sequential) and the update paths 017 also touches.</parallel-reason>
    <deps>017</deps>
    <tags>bff-api, security, testing</tags>
    <estimated-effort>4-6 hours</estimated-effort>
  </metadata>

  <prompt>Make `sprk_ai_search_index` server-owned on every search-indexed table (`RecordTableRules` `SearchIndexed = true`). In `RecordCreationService`, drop a client-supplied value before step 5 (so no AppendTo is asked on the `sprk_aisearchindex` row), and have step 8 (`SearchIndexDefaultAsync`, ~:680/~:1131) apply the index of the record's FINAL owning BU, after the ownership step. An owning BU with no index leaves the column empty and logs `search_index_unset_for_owner_bu`. Apply the same drop on every BFF update/PATCH path that can write the column. Log `client_search_index_dropped` (ids only) when a dropped value differs from the applied one.</prompt>
  <amendment date="2026-10-31" source="owner, in session; notes/decisions.md 2026-10-31 FR-38 widened">Scope is wider than the prompt above: BOTH index columns (sprk_ai_search_index and the legacy text sprk_searchindexname) are server-owned, on SIX tables: mark sprk_workassignment, sprk_event and sprk_invoice SearchIndexed = true in RecordTableRules beside matter, project and document. The drop, the step-8 fill, the update-path drop and the logs apply to both columns on all six. The drop log for the name column also carries the dropped and applied index name (catalog data).</amendment>
  <role>SPAARKE platform developer, .NET 10 BFF, Dataverse write-path security. Follow ADRs strictly.</role>
  <goal>No BFF path lets a client choose a record's search index on a search-indexed table; creates get the final owning BU's index or none; the #2399 refusal (a child-BU caller without AppendTo on a root-owned catalog row) cannot recur through the index column.</goal>

  <context>
    <background>spec.md FR-38 (amends FR-10), design.md §13.1-§13.3b and §13.6 (component justification), notes/decisions.md 2026-10-29 (owner: drop, not refuse; Q2 = (B) canonical rows, no BU defaults). UAC-r2 reviewed the design (conditions 1-4, design §13.3/§13.3b). #2399's live part was fixed by re-owning dev's rows (§13.2 b); this is the durable fix. The wizard side (stop binding the index) is W3 tasks 021-029, not this task.</background>
    <relevant-files>
      <file role="modify">src/server/api/Sprk.Bff.Api/Services/RecordCreation/RecordCreationService.cs (the drop before step 5; step 8 SearchIndexDefaultAsync source = final owning BU; the K3 canonical-key handling from task 018 stays)</file>
      <file role="modify">src/server/api/Sprk.Bff.Api/Services/RecordCreation/RecordTableRules.cs (only if the column needs declaring as server-owned per table; prefer the existing SearchIndexed flag)</file>
      <file role="inventory-then-modify">Every BFF update/PATCH path that can write sprk_ai_search_index on a search-indexed table. Start from: Services/Ai/Handlers/DataverseUpdateRecordHandler.cs, Api/ChildRecordEndpoints.cs (any update route), Api/FieldMappings/FieldMappingEndpoints.cs (push; confirm mapping already protects the column), Api/Events/EventEndpoints.cs, Api/CommunicationEndpoints.cs. Record the inventory (path, table set, verdict) in the task notes.</file>
      <file role="canonical-reference">tests/integration/data-mutation/RecordOwnership/SearchIndexDefaultTests.cs (task 015/018 world; extend or add a sibling class)</file>
      <file role="canonical-reference">018's default_value_dropped log (OfficeService / RecordCreationService) for the log shape</file>
    </relevant-files>
    <dependencies>
      <dependency task="017" status="required">The child-records route and chat create run RecordCreationService, so step 8 covers them.</dependency>
    </dependencies>
  </context>

  <constraints>
    <constraint source="design §13.3 / owner 2026-10-29">Drop, never refuse, a client index. Never fall back to the caller's BU or walk up to the root.</constraint>
    <constraint source="UAC-r2 condition 4">The drop log carries ids only (record, table, dropped index id, applied index id). No names, no emails.</constraint>
    <constraint source="ADR-008 path A">Payload checks stay in the service / CallerWriteAuthorization; route filters unchanged.</constraint>
    <constraint source="ADR-010">No new registration, interface or service.</constraint>
    <constraint source="ADR-038">KEEP paths only (tests/integration/data-mutation/**, tests/unit/domain/**); never tests/unit/Sprk.Bff.Api.Tests/**; no Mock&lt;HttpMessageHandler&gt;.</constraint>
    <constraint source="CLAUDE.md §10">Placement Justification, fresh-master publish-size delta, CVE check in the task notes.</constraint>
  </constraints>

  <knowledge>
    <files>
      <file>projects/field-mapping-server-write-path-r1/design.md (§13)</file>
      <file>projects/field-mapping-server-write-path-r1/spec.md (FR-10, FR-38)</file>
      <file>docs/architecture/DATAVERSE-WRITE-PATH-ARCHITECTURE.md</file>
      <file>.claude/constraints/bff-extensions.md</file>
      <file>.claude/constraints/testing.md</file>
    </files>
  </knowledge>

  <steps mode="directional">
    <step order="1">Inventory the BFF write paths that can set sprk_ai_search_index (see relevant-files); record it in notes/task-039-notes.md.</step>
    <step order="2">Failing tests first (acceptance criteria below).</step>
    <step order="3">Drop before step 5 in the service; step 8 from the final owning BU; logs.</step>
    <step order="4">The same drop on each update path from step 1.</step>
    <step order="5">Build; run the RecordCreation, SearchIndexDefault, CrossSurfaceOwner, SecureChildOwnership* suites (filtered; never the unfiltered Sprk.Bff.Api.Tests) and ArchTests. Publish-size delta; CVE check. Update TASK-INDEX.</step>
  </steps>

  <acceptance-criteria>
    <criterion testable="true">A create carrying a client sprk_ai_search_index on a search-indexed table writes the final owning BU's index (or none) and asks no AppendTo on the catalog row: a caller without AppendTo on it is not refused.</criterion>
    <criterion testable="true">A secure record, and a record whose owning BU has no index, get an empty column and the search_index_unset_for_owner_bu log; no root walk, no caller-BU fallback.</criterion>
    <criterion testable="true">Each BFF update path from the inventory drops a client sprk_ai_search_index on a search-indexed table (one test per path, or a shared helper with one test each).</criterion>
    <criterion testable="true">client_search_index_dropped is logged only when the dropped value differs from the applied one, and carries ids only.</criterion>
    <criterion testable="true">Negative (must-not-fire): on a table that is not search-indexed, a caller-supplied lookup of the same name keeps its AppendTo check and is written.</criterion>
    <criterion testable="true">Task 018's K3 behaviour holds: an explicit null under the lower-case bind key never yields two case-variant keys.</criterion>
    <criterion testable="true">BFF build 0 errors; listed suites and ArchTests pass; publish delta and CVE result recorded.</criterion>
  </acceptance-criteria>

  <justification>
    <existing>FR-10's fill-only default at step 8 (RecordCreationService.SearchIndexDefaultAsync).</existing>
    <extension>Yes: the same step owns the column, plus a drop before step 5 and on the update paths. No new service or file in src.</extension>
    <cost-of-doing-nothing>Every child-BU user's create is refused whenever their BU names an index they cannot AppendTo (#2399), and a client can route a record into another BU's index.</cost-of-doing-nothing>
  </justification>

  <outputs>
    <output type="code">src/server/api/Sprk.Bff.Api/Services/RecordCreation/RecordCreationService.cs</output>
    <output type="code">the update paths from the step-1 inventory</output>
    <output type="test">tests/integration/data-mutation/RecordOwnership/ (server-owned index tests)</output>
    <output type="notes">projects/field-mapping-server-write-path-r1/notes/task-039-notes.md</output>
  </outputs>

  <notes>Added 2026-10-30 by the scope procedure (design §13 → UAC-r2 review → spec FR-38 → this task → TASK-INDEX → owner approval). Release note: a client can no longer choose a record's search index; records land in their owning BU's index. Wizard cleanup is 021-029 (design §13.2 e).

COMPLETED 2026-11-01: PR #2504 merged as 0e3962069b (09:50:31Z). Scope widened by the owner before start (decisions.md 2026-10-31): six tables (+ work assignment, event, invoice SearchIndexed) and both columns (sprk_ai_search_index + sprk_searchindexname); step 8 is the only writer on the create/client paths. Update paths drop through one helper, RecordTableRules.DropSearchIndexFromUpdate (inventory of 13 paths in notes/task-039-notes.md); a new ArchTest, SearchIndexDropGuardTests. Final verification: build 0/0; ArchTests 1887; filtered 6553 passed, 7 skipped, 0 failed; publish +7,832 B against a fresh master f56cf8f724 (39.10 MB); CVE none. Reviews: one Opus adversarial pass (0 BLOCKING; 6 fix-now + docs, fixed); a scoped Sonnet re-check (4 small findings, fixed); code-review + adr-check (nothing Critical, no ADR violation; 5 fix-now, fixed). UAC-r2 reviewed at d90098ade8: no blocking findings, K5 accepted. ebilling: no objection to the sprk_invoice flag. Known limits K1-K12 in the notes; filed: #2502 / DI-012 (rag/index-file names the index; owner decision); #2413 gained the 195 moves as a known instance. Not live: ships with the next batched dev BFF deploy (task 019).
rework: fix-round-3 task 039</notes>

